      "description": "Staff Search Page social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Staff We're Hiring! Search All Jobs Skip to jobs search results Clear Filters Category Search categories 11 filter options found Category Academic/Student Support (6 items) 6 Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer (1 items) 1 Athletics (1 items) 1 Aviation (27 items) 27 Facilities/Groundskeeping (1 items) 1 Finance (1 items) 1 Information Technology (3 items) 3 Management/Administration (6 items) 6 Office/Administrative Support (5 items) 5 Staff (70 items) 70 Temporary (1 items) 1 Department(s) Search 18 filter options found Department(s) Academic Affairs Direct (1 items) 1 Administrative and Support (1 items) 1 Barton School of Business (2 items) 2 College of Education (1 items) 1 College of Engineering (1 items) 1 Culture and HR (2 items) 2 Finance Administration (College) (1 items) 1 Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm (3 items) 3 NIAR Institute (26 items) 26 Office Ind & Defense Administration (8 items) 8 Office of CivilRights,TitleIX & ADA (1 items) 1 Office of Research (College) (2 items) 2 Physical Plant (7 items) 7 Strategic Communications (1 items) 1 Strategic Engagement & Planning (9 items) 9 Strategic Enrollment Mgmt (2 items) 2 Student Affairs (College) (1 items) 1 WSU Police Department (2 items) 2 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Sort by: Last Updated Last Updated: Newest to Oldest Last Updated: Oldest to Newest Title: A-Z Title: Z-A NIAR Program Manager I - Sustainment 499590 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute NIAR Sustainment is seeking an experienced and highly motivated Program Manager to join our team in Park City, KS. In this role, you will lead and support cross‑functional project teams, ensuring the successful execution of laboratory research, testing, and program activities. This position offers the opportunity to work in a fast‑paced, hands‑on environment where collaboration, technical aptitude, and strong program oversight are key. If you’re driven to deliver results, excel at managing complex program requirements, and thrive in a team‑oriented setting, we invite you to apply. Read more Senior Investigator- Civil Rights & Title IX 499501 Wichita Staff Office of CivilRights,TitleIX & ADA The Role: Objective Investigation & Policy Compliance\n\nWe are seeking a precise, analytical professional to join our team as a Civil Rights and Title IX Investigator. In this role, you will serve as a neutral fact-finder, managing complex cases and ensuring strict compliance with institutional policies and federal regulations. Read more Financial Aid Advisor 499474 Wichita Academic/Student Support Staff Strategic Enrollment Mgmt Are you ready to make a difference in the lives of students? We’re looking for an energetic, empathetic person to join our Student Impact Team -- someone who’s excited to help students navigate financial aid, scholarships, loans, and their overall financial wellness.\n\nIn this role, you’ll do more than process paperwork. You’ll meet with students and families, respond to cases and emails, and collaborate with partners across campus. You’ll listen closely, identify what students truly need, and help them understand the options available to them. Read more Maintenance Technician, Senior 499331 Wichita Staff Physical Plant As a Senior Maintenance Technician, you're one of the key people who helps keep everything running smoothly behind the scenes. Part organizer, part problem-solver, and part efficiency expert, you ensure materials, equipment, and supplies are where they need to be, when they need to be there. From managing inventory and tracking resources to organizing equipment and supporting workflow planning, you help create the structure that allows the entire operation to succeed.\n\nYou'll use powered industrial equipment to safely move materials throughout the facility, assist with the staging and tracking of assets and supplies, and maintain accurate records that help keep operations organized and efficient. When stock levels need attention or resources need to be coordinated, you're ready to step in and make sure nothing falls through the cracks.\n\nYour impact extends beyond materials and inventory. You help keep the facility safe, functional, and well-maintained through routine building maintenance, minor repairs, preventive maintenance activities, equipment inspections, and general upkeep of facility systems and infrastructure. Whether responding to service requests, addressing everyday maintenance needs, or supporting seasonal snow and ice removal efforts, you take pride in helping create an environment where people can do their best work.\n\nSuccess in this role comes from attention to detail, a commitment to safety, and a proactive approach to continuous improvement. You enjoy finding ways to make things more organized, efficient, and reliable, and you take pride in being a trusted team member who helps keep both operations and facilities running at their best. Read more IDP Project Coordinator - Advanced Materials Research 499643 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute Join the innovative team at NIAR’s Advanced Materials Research group and help drive cutting‑edge projects that shape the future of aerospace and advanced manufacturing. We’re looking for a proactive Project Manager who thrives in a collaborative, fast‑paced environment and enjoys turning complex ideas into successful, well‑executed outcomes. If you’re motivated by meaningful work, enjoy partnering with experts across disciplines, and want to be part of a mission-focused research organization, we’d love to hear from you. Read more Custodial Lead 499392 Wichita Staff Physical Plant Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Lead, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment. And the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. Read more Custodial Supervisor, Second Shift 499396 Wichita Staff Physical Plant Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Supervisor, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment.\n\nAnd the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. Read more Custodian Specialist, Senior 499389 Wichita Staff Physical Plant When campus floors need expert care and cleaning equipment needs a skilled hand, our Custodian Specialist, Senior steps in to make it happen.\n\nYou’re the kind of person who takes pride in a gleaming hallway, a freshly waxed floor, and a vacuum that hums like new. You know your way around scrubbers, buffers, and carpet extractors, and when something breaks, you don’t just report it, you help fix it. You research parts and coordinate repairs to keep our custodial equipment running like a dream. Read more Custodian, Special Events and Projects 499391 Wichita Staff Physical Plant The Custodian of Special Events and Projects plays a key role in keeping the WSU campus clean, disinfected, and safe while supporting the energetic flow of athletic, community, and special events that bring the university to life. This dynamic position adapts to shifting schedules, including weekends, evenings, and nontraditional hours, to ensure every event shines, from packed athletic games to campus wide celebrations. In addition to event support, this role also contributes to important campus projects such as floor refinishing, carpet extraction, deep restroom sanitization, and seasonal maintenance tasks that keep facilities in top condition. The position also champions environmentally conscious “green” cleaning practices, helping create healthier spaces for students, staff, and visitors. With a robust benefits package effective on day one, generous paid time off, and the opportunity to directly support WSU’s most memorable moments, this role offers both meaningful impact and rewarding flexibility. Read more Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior 499394 Wichita Staff Physical Plant We are excited to announce an opportunity for a Senior Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist to join our university community and play a vital role in fostering a safe, healthy, and compliant campus environment. This position coordinates with various areas to complete assigned environmental health and safety functions and inspections. Provides guidance and assistance and is responsible for promoting a safe and healthy workplace. Implements plans based on contracts, regulations, applicable laws and audit/inspection results to ensure that compliance is maintained. May provide training to employees in areas including, but not limited to, environmental, health and safety management best practices, and assisting with hazard identification and control. Read more Director Support Services- Postal, Printing & Promo Solutions 499341 Wichita Management/Administration Staff Finance Administration (College) Some days you’ll be the face of the operation. Other days, you’ll be the person behind the curtain making sure everything works.\n\nYou’ll lead the daily operations of the department. We need someone who can look at the operation & evaluate:\nWhat’s working?\nWhat isn't?\nWhat do we need next?\nAnd how can we do this better? Read more NIAR 5-Axis CNC Machinist 499480 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute The National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) at Wichita State University is looking for an experienced Multi-Axis Machinist.  This position is located at the Advanced Machining and Prototyping (AMP) Lab in Park City, KS.  \nIf you are someone that takes pride in your work and will work to push the needle forward to meet customers' requirements, apply now!  Come join our fast-paced and fast-growing team! Read more Landscaper 498900 Wichita Facilities/Groundskeeping Staff Physical Plant Do you enjoy working outside? This Landscaper position provides opportunities to work outdoors as a member of a supportive team and have daily duties that vary according to University need. This position also comes with a robust benefits package (effective on your first day) and generous paid time off. Read more Employee Relations Specialist- HR 499409 Wichita Staff Culture and HR Workplace challenges are rarely black and white. We’re looking for an experienced Employee Relations/HR professional who can navigate complex situations with curiosity, sound judgment, and a commitment to fairness. Read more NIAR CNC Machinist II - ATLAS 499550 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute Join the NIAR ATLAS team and play a key role in shaping precision manufacturing at Wichita State University. We’re looking for a skilled CNC Machinist who enjoys hands-on work, solving problems, and transforming detailed technical designs into exact, high‑quality components. If you thrive in an environment where craftsmanship, accuracy, and continuous improvement are valued, this full-time, on-site role offers the opportunity to grow your expertise while contributing to innovative research and production. Read more Community Program Coordinator 499108 Wichita Office/Administrative Support Staff Strategic Engagement & Planning Are you an organized multitasker who thrives on bringing people, projects, and ideas together? Do you enjoy researching solutions, analyzing information, engaging with community partners, and helping meaningful initiatives move from concept to completion? If so, we want to hear from you. Read more NIAR CNC Machinist I - ATLAS 499545 Wichita Staff NIAR Institute Join the NIAR ATLAS team and play a key role in shaping precision manufacturing at Wichita State University. We’re looking for a skilled CNC Machinist who enjoys hands-on work, solving problems, and transforming detailed technical designs into exact, high‑quality components. If you thrive in an environment where craftsmanship, accuracy, and continuous improvement are valued, this full-time, on-site role offers the opportunity to grow your expertise while contributing to innovative research and production. Read more NIAR Liaison Engineer - Sustainment 499195 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute NIAR Sustainment is hiring a full-time engineering liaison to support customer communication, interpret technical data, and provide recommendations based on inspection results. This role prepares technical reports, supports root cause analysis, and participates in technical discussions. U.S. citizenship is required due to export-controlled work. Work is performed onsite in our Park City location. Read more NIAR Executive Assistant 499497 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute The Administrative Professional plays a vital role in supporting senior leadership within NIAR Sustainment by ensuring seamless coordination of daily operations and strategic activities. This position manages complex calendars, organizes high‑level meetings and events, arranges domestic and international travel, and prepares clear, well‑crafted correspondence, presentations, and reports that support informed decision‑making. Read more Commencement & Events Coordinator 498431 Wichita Staff Academic Affairs Direct Wichita State University is seeking a highly organized and detail-oriented Commencement & Events Coordinator to join our team of event professionals. This position will plan, coordinate, and execute commencement ceremonies and other University events for WSU campus and community. This role plays a critical part in ensuring high-quality experiences by coordinating logistics, facilities, services, and on-site operations. Read more Digital and Video Producer 499268 Wichita Academic/Student Support Management/Administration Office/Administrative Support Staff Show More Show Less Strategic Communications Are you a creative storyteller who thrives behind the camera, in the editing suite and at the design desk? Wichita State University is seeking a talented Digital and Video Producer to help bring the university’s stories to life through compelling visual content.\nAs part of the Office of Strategic Communications and Marketing, this hybrid creative role will produce high-quality video content and support a wide range of visual design initiatives that enhance the university’s brand and engage diverse audiences. Reporting to the Director of Videography, the successful candidate will collaborate with campus partners to create content that informs, inspires and connects the Wichita State community. Read more Placement and Office Coordinator 499293 Wichita Staff College of Education If you enjoy building relationships, keeping complex processes organized, and helping students succeed, this role offers an opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the preparation of future educators.\n\nAs the Placement and Office Coordinator in the College of Education, you will serve as a central connection between students, faculty, school district partners, and university staff to ensure high-quality field and clinical experiences. You will coordinate educational placements, monitor student readiness and compliance with program requirements, and help ensure that accreditation standards, university policies, and partnership agreements are met.\n\nSuccess in this position requires someone who is highly organized, proactive, and detail oriented. You will communicate regularly with students, faculty, and external partners, identify opportunities to strengthen placement processes and services, and help maintain strong relationships with school districts and community partners. Your work will directly contribute to creating meaningful experiential learning opportunities for future educators. Read more IDP Technology HelpDesk Specialist 499415 Wichita Information Technology Staff Office Ind & Defense Administration Join the IDP Information Technology Center at Wichita State University and help empower students and staff with reliable, high‑quality technology support. In this hands‑on role, you’ll be the go‑to problem solver for end‑user devices, ensuring our campus community stays productive and connected. If you’re passionate about troubleshooting, enjoy helping others, and are ready to grow your IT career in a dynamic environment, we’d love to meet you. Read more NIAR Program Manager - ATLAS 499441 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute ATLAS is looking for a Program Manager with a good understanding of material and process specifications, manufacturing techniques, and certification and qualification testing for advanced composites materials. Read more IDP Information Security Analyst 499416 Wichita Information Technology Staff Office Ind & Defense Administration WSU IDP is currently searching for a Cybersecurity Analyst to assist with NIAR’s Security Helpdesk and Operations Center (SHOC). The SHOC is responsible for monitoring and safeguarding the organization’s systems and data, as well as enforcing cybersecurity industry best practices and compliance with NIST 800-171. The SHOC also plays a support and collaborative role with other WSU InfoSec teams. Read more Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist 499112 Wichita Staff Office of Research (College) In this senior-level role, you will provide comprehensive pre-award support for primarily grant and contract applications submitted on behalf of Wichita State University. Are you a problem solver? Enjoy the challenge of multiple projects and meeting their deadlines? This position will be responsible for the development, implementation and oversight of pre-award grant and contract functions, including ensuring all applications comply with sponsor and University guidelines, and State and Federal rules and regulations. In this role, you will be part of a team that makes it possible for Wichita State and our industry partners to conduct research and projects that will improve and change the community of Wichita, health, education, and technology for Kansas, the US and possibly the world! Read more IDP Export Control Manager 499363 Wichita Staff Office Ind & Defense Administration Join a dynamic research environment where innovation meets compliance. The Export Control Manager serves as a trusted expert and key partner across the university, ensuring groundbreaking research and global collaborations align with federal export control regulations. In this role, you’ll shape and lead the university’s export control program, advise faculty and researchers on complex regulatory requirements, manage critical licensing processes, and maintain the university’s ITAR registration. If you’re energized by problem‑solving, collaboration, and supporting research that pushes boundaries, this position offers a meaningful opportunity to make an impact. Read more NIAR Aerospace Painter - Composites 499057 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute The Aerospace Painter and Laboratory Technician supports NIAR Composites by preparing surfaces, mixing and applying aerospace coatings, and conducting performance and flammability testing in accordance with industry and FAA standards. The role also assists with laboratory operations, equipment maintenance, hazardous waste handling, and training of students on safe and proper procedures. Read more Program Counselor, College Readiness/Retention Programs 498700 Wichita Staff Strategic Engagement & Planning Be the Reason a Student Says, “I’m Going to College.”\n\nIf you’re the kind of person who sees potential before others do…\nIf you believe access to education shouldn’t depend on zip code…\nIf you’re energized by mentoring youth and watching confidence grow in real time…\n\nTRIO Talent Search is looking for you!\n\nAssigned Schools:\nMarshall Middle School and North High School (plus walk-in support as needed)\n\nThis isn’t a desk job. It’s boots-on-the-ground, sleeves-rolled-up, future-building work. You’ll work directly with middle and high school students, many of whom will be first-generation college students, guiding them toward academic persistence, high school graduation, and postsecondary enrollment. You’ll serve approximately 290 students annually, ensuring each one receives meaningful, documented, and compliant federal TRIO services. The heart of this job? Relationships.\n\nWhat You’ll Actually Be Doing:\nCollaborate with school administrators and community partners\nIdentify eligible students for the program & monitor their academic progress (intervening when needed)\nBuilding partnerships & relationships along the way at various levels\nMaintaining accurate student records and ensuring federal compliance\nYes, there’s documentation — because impact matters, and so does accountability.\n\nYou'll Thrive Here If You:\nConnect easily with youth across diverse backgrounds\nKnow how to balance encouragement with structure\nCan pivot quickly when student needs shift (because they will)\nAre organized enough to manage data while staying fully present with students\nUnderstand referral networks and aren’t afraid to collaborate\nBelieve that mentorship can literally change a life trajectory\nYou are intentional. Strategic. Consistent.\n\nIn a world where conversations about equity, opportunity gaps, and educational access dominate headlines, this is where the real work happens, one student at a time. If you’re ready to build futures, we want to hear from you.\nApply. Mentor. Advocate. Change trajectories! Read more Veterans Academic Advisor- Veterans Upward Bound 499054 Wichita Academic/Student Support Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer Management/Administration Office/Administrative Support Staff Show More Show Less Strategic Engagement & Planning Your Mission\n\nYou’ll work exclusively with military-affiliated students, providing wraparound services, start-to-finish support, from certification of benefits to graduation and beyond. When veteran and military-affiliated students transition into college life, they often face unique challenges related to academic planning, benefit navigation, and adjustment to civilian and campus culture. This role provides individualized academic guidance and support to help these students succeed. This is not a transactional advising role. You’ll serve as a constant throughout a student’s academic journey; someone they can trust to help them navigate both higher education systems and other military benefit programs with clarity and care. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 71 in total ‹ 1 2 3 › 1845 Fairmount St. Wichita , Kansas 67260 USA (316) 978-3456 Request Info Visit Apply Contact Us Virtual Tour Campus Map and Directions Facebook X | Twitter Instagram YouTube Linkedin People at Wichita State will make introductions, look for (applied learning) opportunities, and give advice that will put you miles ahead of others. Jon Peterson , senior in business administration and real estate finance Alumni & Friends Give to WSU A-Z Index Freedom of Expression Policies and Procedures Privacy Policy Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Campus Safety Accessibility Public Information Website Support KBOR Freedom of Expression Statement HLC Accreditation © 2024 Wichita State University Wichita State University (\"WSU\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs, activities, admissions and employment. Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://internal-jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/search": {
      "title": "If you are not a current employee, please visit our external careers page at: jobs.wichita.edu",
      "description": "Internal Careers Employee Job Listing social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode You have reached the internal side of Wichita State University's Careers Page. Positions advertised on the internal site are only available to employees of Wichita State or ICAA. Please click the button below and be prepared to log in with your WSU credentials to view these roles. Click for Internal Roles If you are not a current employee, please visit our external careers page at: jobs.wichita.edu 1845 Fairmount St. Wichita , Kansas 67260 USA (316) 978-3456 Request Info Visit Apply Contact Us Virtual Tour Campus Map and Directions Facebook X | Twitter Instagram YouTube Linkedin People at Wichita State will make introductions, look for (applied learning) opportunities, and give advice that will put you miles ahead of others. Jon Peterson , senior in business administration and real estate finance Alumni & Friends Give to WSU A-Z Index Freedom of Expression Policies and Procedures Privacy Policy Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Campus Safety Accessibility Public Information Website Support KBOR Freedom of Expression Statement HLC Accreditation © 2024 Wichita State University Wichita State University (\"WSU\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs, activities, admissions and employment. Candidate Details"
