unity to work in a fast‑paced, hands‑on environment where collaboration, technical aptitude, and strong program oversight are key. If you’re driven to deliver results, excel at managing complex program requirements, and thrive in a team‑oriented setting, we invite you to apply. Senior Investigator- Civil Rights & Title IX The Role: Objective Investigation & Policy Compliance\n\nWe are seeking a precise, analytical professional to join our team as a Civil Rights and Title IX Investigator. In this role, you will serve as a neutral fact-finder, managing complex cases and ensuring strict compliance with institutional policies and federal regulations. 1845 Fairmount St. Wichita , Kansas 67260 USA (316) 978-3456 Request Info Visit Apply Contact Us Virtual Tour Campus Map and Directions Facebook X | Twitter Instagram YouTube Linkedin People at Wichita State will make introductions, look for (applied learning) opportunities, and give advice that will put you miles ahead of others. Jon Peterson , senior in business administration and real estate finance Alumni & Friends Give to WSU A-Z Index Freedom of Expression Policies and Procedures Privacy Policy Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Campus Safety Accessibility Public Information Website Support KBOR Freedom of Expression Statement HLC Accreditation © 2024 Wichita State University Wichita State University (\"WSU\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs, activities, admissions and employment. Not sure if Wichita is right for you?  Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 0f201234 Last Name (required) 2cfc2a8b Email (required) c380a9ad Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe a