    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/maintenance-technician-senior-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician, Senior",
      "description": "Maintenance Technician, Senior - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Maintenance Technician, Senior Physical Plant | Staff Maintenance Technician, Senior 499331 Staff Add to favorites View favorites Department: Facilities Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starting at $23.67 and commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 7:45 am - 4:30 pm Monday - Friday; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story As a Senior Maintenance Technician, you are the expert problem-solver who keeps our facilities, equipment, and operations running safely and efficiently. From installing, inspecting, and repairing complex mechanical systems to tackling escalated troubleshooting issues, you play a critical role in minimizing downtime and maintaining reliability. You work independently and collaboratively to complete structural and utility repairs, manage materials and inventory, maintain accurate service records, and respond to seasonal needs such as snow and ice removal. Your technical expertise, attention to detail, and commitment to excellence help create a safe, functional, and well-maintained environment for everyone. Job Summary Performs preventive and corrective maintenance of complex equipment and systems throughout the facility. Essential Functions Installs, tests, maintains and repairs mechanical machinery, equipment and systems as scheduled or needed. Performs utility and structural repairs as needed, alone or in collaboration with internal and/or external trades. Inspects and tests equipment. Documents and maintains records of inspections and work performed pursuant to departmental policies and warranty and/or vendor requirements. Requisitions materials and supplies, maintains inventory Performs troubleshooting or repairs that have been escalated or that are more complex. Shovels and removes snow and ice from designated areas such as roofs, sidewalks and entryways as required. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Four (4) years of experience in general maintenance Required License/Certifications/Training: Valid Driver's License Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to gain knowledge of work-related agency operations, safety standards and procedures. Ability to understand and follow explicit instructions, both in oral and written form. Ability to work effectively with fellow workers and others. Ability to assist others as needed. Physical Requirements: Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Frequent 60-90% Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Frequent 60-90% Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify any errors, needs, and/or determining factors. Occasional 30-60% Ability to remain in a stationary position. Rare 0-30% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Rare 0-30% Ability to drive state vehicle. Rare 0-30% Ability to remove snow and ice from designated areas. Rare 0-30% Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Rare 0-30% Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) 70c84812 Last Name (required) 2e0e0b7e Email (required) 6861de26 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 12257e8a Last Name (required) aac9fd6d Email (required) 0c0cadfb Job Alert 44e43077 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Physical Plant Physical Plant Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) e812954a Last Name (required) 483e2ccb Email (required) 2c8cf9cd Send This Job To: daf986cb Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available).