    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/idp-project-coordinator-advanced-materials-research-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "IDP Project Coordinator",
      "description": "IDP Project Coordinator - Advanced Materials Research - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode IDP Project Coordinator - Advanced Materials Research NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff IDP Project Coordinator - Advanced Materials Research 499643 Aviation Staff Add to favorites View favorites Department: NIAR Advanced Materials Research Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Monday - Friday; work is performed onsite and in-person.;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Information Join the innovative team at NIAR’s Advanced Materials Research group and help drive cutting‑edge projects that shape the future of aerospace and advanced manufacturing. We’re looking for a proactive Project Coordinator who thrives in a collaborative, fast‑paced environment and enjoys turning complex ideas into successful, well‑executed outcomes. If you’re motivated by meaningful work, enjoy partnering with experts across disciplines, and want to be part of a mission-focused research organization, we’d love to hear from you. Job Summary Manages assigned project(s) to meet department objectives. Essential Functions Develops project plans, creates schedules and ensures task deliverables meet expectations. Collaborates with project contributors to assess and ensure successful project outcomes. Defines and ensures resources are assigned to meet project goals. Monitors project and communicates quality and progress metrics to department and/or staff(s). Recommends project budget and monitors and adjusts plan as resource requirements change. Addresses and resolves project issues to ensure goals remain on track. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college coursework in business administration or related field. Four (4) years of experience in project management or related field. Every 30 hours of college coursework beyond 60 hours can be substituted for one (1) year of experience, up to 120 hours. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of project management principles, scheduling, and resource planning. Knowledge of budgeting practices and project performance metrics. Skill in coordinating teams and ensuring project deliverables meet expectations. Skill in identifying issues, mitigating risks, and maintaining project timelines. Skill in clear, professional communication with staff and stakeholders. Ability to manage multiple projects and adapt to changing requirements. Ability to interpret project specifications and apply departmental objectives. Ability to meet U.S. export compliance requirements (EAR/ITAR). Physical Requirements: Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Apply Now First Name (required) 3defd8bd Last Name (required) 7b1f4db0 Email (required) fb9efae0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form an