    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-it-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR IT Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR IT Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode NIAR IT Student Assistant Office Ind & Defense Administration | Student NIAR IT Student Assistant 495589 Student Favorited View favorites Department NIAR Information Technology Center Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $12.50 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The Information Technology Center is looking for an IT student assistant to help with daily tasks such as software and hardware installs, phone support as well as onsite, troubleshooting, and documentation. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Software\\Hardware installs • Phone and onsite support • Software\\Hardware troubleshooting • Researching resolutions for computer problems • Documentation • Tasks as assigned • Must have a good understanding of MS Windows (operations and networking) • Ability to work in a team and individually • Ability to explain technical issues in a non-technical way to an End User • Task and detailed orientated Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Information for Posting Lifting, moving hardware, getting behind and under desks/cubicles Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) b10a87b4 Last Name (required) b7a2dacd Email (required) e55d6f7d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ce8f5cae Last Name (required) fb47b29b Email (required) df8bccd0 Job Alert e7d3104a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Office Ind & Defense Administration Office Ind & Defense Administration Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) d616505d Last Name (require