    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/drth-embedded-security-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "DRTH Embedded Security Student Assistant",
      "description": "DRTH Embedded Security Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode DRTH Embedded Security Student Assistant Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student DRTH Embedded Security Student Assistant 499405 Student Add to favorites View favorites Department Digital Research Transformation Hub Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 22 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The Embedded Security Student Assistant will work directly with the research development team to support the design and implementation of security assessments for embedded devices. This role offers hands-on experience with AI-assisted penetration testing, reverse engineering, and standardized security frameworks. The ideal candidate will contribute to finding vulnerabilities and developing proof-of-concept exploits while learning standardized frameworks and low-level functionality of embedded systems. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Assist in designing and developing attacks against commercial off the shelf embedded devices. • Support research into state-of-the-art attacks and security frameworks. • Help develop AI-assisted security assessments. • Support integration of AI models into security assessments. • Participate in code reviews and documentation of technical solutions. • Assist with monitoring, logging, and optimization of embedded devices. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements • Pursuing a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree. • Excellent communication skills and ability to work in a team environment. • Self-motivated with ability to learn new technologies quickly with minimal supervision. • Ability to work with and understand complex systems. • Basic understanding of Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Cyber Security, embedded systems, interest in a career in these areas. • Strong organizational and time-management skills. • Strong problem-solving and analytical thinking abilities. • Enthusiastic and willing to learn from a variety of specialists in the fields of AI/ML, IoT, and intelligent manufacturing. • Working knowledge of general-purpose programming languages such as C/C++ and Python. • Basic understanding of cybersecurity concepts. • Must be able to work a minimum of 20 hours a week. Preferred Qualifications • Preference for completion of at least one cybersecurity course and one programming course. • Experience building embedded device systems such as a Raspberry Pi or Arduino based solution. • Familiarity with the ATT&CK Framework. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) d15fba41 Last Name (required) b4acc8ff Email (required) 89af0243 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 68fa771e Last Name (required) 7ba69031 Email (required) 2447d2ab Job Alert b25cbd37 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 1145a837 Last Name (required) fdbb3b4f Email (required) f7a21bb3 Send This Job To: a40d9503 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended J