    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-atlas-testing-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR ATLAS Testing Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR ATLAS Testing Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode NIAR ATLAS Testing Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR ATLAS Testing Student Assistant 497160 Student Add to favorites View favorites Department NIAR ATLAS Lab Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - $18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The NIAR ATLAS lab is looking for a student assistant to help with testing and data analysis. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Assist in setting up and conducting composite mechanical testing and data analysis in accordance with standardized procedures. Capable of independently completing assigned tasks while ensuring clear and consistent communication with the supervisor and research teams. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Requirements Must be currently enrolled in an undergradua