    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/drth-human-factors-in-cybersecurity-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "DRTH Human Factors in Cybersecurity Student Assistant",
      "description": "DRTH Human Factors in Cybersecurity Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode DRTH Human Factors in Cybersecurity Student Assistant Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student DRTH Human Factors in Cybersecurity Student Assistant 499404 Student Add to favorites View favorites Department Digital Research Transformation Hub Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 22 per hour Work Schedule Based of class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The Human Factors in Cybersecurity Student Assistant will work directly with the research development team to support the design and implementation of human subject experiments. This role offers hands-on experience with designing and implementing web interfaces, designing surveys, and analyzing data. The ideal candidate will contribute to the design and execution of experiments with human subjects. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties • Assist in designing and developing Web interfaces following human factors principles. • Support research into state-of-the-art methods for human factors in cybersecurity. • Help develop surveys for human subject experiments. • Participate in documentation of technical solutions. • Assist with data collection and data analysis. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements • Pursuing a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree. • Excellent communication skills and ability to work in a team environment. • Self-motivated with ability to learn new technologies quickly with minimal supervision. • Ability to work with and understand complex systems. • Basic understanding of statistical analysis, human factors, and cybersecurity principles. • Strong organizational and time-management skills. • Strong problem-solving and analytical thinking abilities. • Enthusiastic and willing to learn from a variety of specialists in the fields of human factors, AI/ML, IoT, and cybersecurity. • Working knowledge of general-purpose programming languages such as Python. • Must be able to work a minimum of 20 hours a week. Preferred Qualifications • Preference for completion of at least one cybersecurity course and one human factors course. • Experience building websites or other coding projects. • Familiarity with statistical analysis such ANOVA. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 3f25eb30 Last Name (required) c85c2149 Email (required) 05077730 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  M