    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-apex-engineering-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR APEX Engineering Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR APEX Engineering Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode NIAR APEX Engineering Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR APEX Engineering Student Assistant 499043 Student Add to favorites View favorites Department NIAR APEX Advanced Prod Execution Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 20 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story NIAR’s APEX lab is looking for students to work with multiple lab capabilities for various projects at HAMR. Students may be required to learn about CAD and other software products and hardware. They will support a variety of projects and programs for the lab. Their task may range from classroom support and project research to direct industry program support. Employees will be expected to assist lab staff in any way possible to help make the lab successful, presentable to customers, and accomplish projects in a timely manner. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties · Support staff with reverse engineering projects. · Interpret existing engineering and quality data. · Model components from various data sources. · Assist staff with research project development. · Assisting staff on the industry level support. · Operate and help maintain tools and equipment. · Help keep a clean and safe work environment. · Assisting staff with the development of training materials. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications · Experience utilizing a CAD software program. · Excellent oral and written communication skills. · Proficiency with Microsoft Office Products. · Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings and bill of material systems. · Have great attention to detail. · Ability to lift and carry up to 25lbs. · Ability to work with complex systems. · Able to work 20+ hours each week. · Effectively prioritize and manage workflow. · Ability to work independently on extensive tasks. Additional Information Students must have their own transportation, as some local travel between facilities may be required. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 48626372 Last Name (required) 33a57492 Email (required) 2ad35634 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 49c17b64 Last Name (requir