      "title": "JAKS Construction Coordinator Student Assistant",
      "description": "JAKS Construction Coordinator Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode JAKS Construction Coordinator Student Assistant Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Student JAKS Construction Coordinator Student Assistant 499287 Student Add to favorites View favorites Department Ennovar Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story Ennovar is looking for a Student Assistant Coordinator to work at JAKS Construction. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties * Assist with creating and maintaining project schedules, task lists, and documentation in JobTread. * Coordinate with subcontractors and suppliers regarding project timelines, deliveries, quotes, and required documents. * Participate in site visits and inspections and help maintain daily logs, project photos, and progress updates. * Support the completion of punch lists, closeout documents, and client communications. * Assist with quantity takeoffs using project plans and specifications. * Request, collect, and organize subcontractor and supplier pricing. * Help prepare project estimates and maintain current material pricing information. * Assist with developing scopes of work, proposals, and presentation materials. * Support lead intake, follow-up, and organization of the sales pipeline. * Attend networking and community events with team members. * Help collect client reviews, referrals, and testimonials. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications * Currently pursuing or recently completed a degree in Construction Management, Engineering, Business, or a related field; equivalent hands-on experience or interest in the trades may be considered. * Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to follow through on assigned tasks. * Ability and willingness to learn new software, including JobTread, spreadsheets, and email platforms. * Strong written and verbal communication skills. * Reliable, self-motivated, coach-able, and able to work both independently and collaboratively. * Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation required for travel to customer and project sites. * Ability to work on active job sites, including walking, standing, occasional lifting, and exposure to varying weather conditions. Additional Information Work is performed on site at JAKS Construction 5025 E Kellogg Dr. Wichita, KS Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 3ff3babb Last Name (required) ee8b32fc Email (required) 6805273c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 64fb285a Last Name (required) d998d411 Email (required) d21d5f36 Job Alert 69fa8f57 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) c7fd6ba8 Last Name (required) 2b01c574 Email (required) f645b2b9 Send This Job To: 91e33e25 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. NIAR Full Scale Facilities Student Assistant The NIAR Full Scale Structural Test lab is looking for a Facilities Student Assistant. NIAR Program Manager I - Sustainment NIAR Sustainment is seeking an experienced and highly motivated Program Manager to join our team in Park City, KS. In this role, you will lead and support cross‑functional project teams, ensuring the successful execution of laboratory research, testing, and program activities. This position offers the opportunity to work in a fast‑paced, hands‑on environment where collaboration, technical aptitude, and strong program oversight are key. If you’re driven to deliver results, excel at managing complex program requirements, and thrive in a team‑oriented setting, we invite you to apply. Senior Investigator- Civil Rights & Title IX The Role: Objective Investigation & Policy Compliance\n\nWe are seeking a precise, analytical professional to join our team as a Civil Rights and Title IX Investigator. In this role, you will serve as a neutral fact-finder, managing complex cases and ensuring strict compliance with institutional policies and federal regulations. 1845 Fairmount St. Wichita , Kansas 67260 USA (316) 978-3456 Request Info Visit Apply Contact Us Virtual Tour Campus Map and Directions Facebook X | Twitter Instagram YouTube Linkedin People at Wichita State will make introductions, look for (applied learning) opportunities, and give advice that will put you miles ahead of others. Jon Peterson , senior in business administration and real estate finance Alumni & Friends Give to WSU A-Z Index Freedom of Expression Policies and Procedures Privacy Policy Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Campus Safety Accessibility Public Information Website Support KBOR Freedom of Expression Statement HLC Accreditation © 2024 Wichita State University Wichita State University (\"WSU\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs, activities, admissions and employment. Not sure if Wichita is right for you?  Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) c5b4b2ca Last Name (required) 4df2ee62 Email (required) a88b9fc9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
